I think one way to do this would be use `rewrites` in the config file (next.config.js)

Something like:

```ts
import type { NextConfig } from "next";

const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  async rewrites() {
    return [
      {
        source: "/send-money-to-:country(\\w+)/:rest*",
        destination: "/send-money-to/:country/:rest*",
      },
    ];
  },
};

export default nextConfig;
```

Which yes, still requires you to re-organize `/send-money-to-[country]/[bank].js` into `/send-money-to/[country]/[bank].js` but for your users, the URL can still be `/send-money-to-foo/bar`.

